    {
      "note": "Substantival article governing a prepositional phrase. A prepositional phrase has no verb to carry a supplied relativizer, so the article keeps 'which' along with the determiner and nominal the English brings (rules 31, 32); rule 22 keeps the head on the nominal word rather than the determiner or the relativizer. Giving 'which' to πρός was the earlier reading, but rule 62's τὴν παρὰ τοῦ μόνου θεοῦ → that cometh from the only God leaves the relativizer with the article and only the supplied verb with the preposition.",
